  {
   "id": 640155,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/665b84386589b9dd.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Tomotari Mitsuoka/Chounaisaikin_no_hanashi, Iwanami Shoten, Publishers)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>This graph shows the number of bacteria in different parts of the human digestive system. Each line shows a separate bacteria species.</p>\n<p>Which statement is correct?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1248122,
     "content_html": "The stomach does not have any bacteria."
    },
    {
     "id": 1248121,
     "content_html": "Bifidobacterium is found in the mouth and the stomach."
    },
    {
     "id": 1248123,
     "content_html": "Escherichia coli (E. coli) is found mostly in the colon and the rectum."
    },
    {
     "id": 1248120,
     "content_html": "Streptococcus is found in highest numbers in the mouth."
    }
   ],
